# Long-running data scripts

Scripts that iterate over hundreds or thousands of items (extract, transform, publish, apply) **must** log progress to stdout so operators can tell the job is alive.

## Requirements

- Log at start: total count and key flags (`--force`, `--dry-run`, `--only`).
- Log periodically during the loop (every **50** items, or every **10** for slow network I/O).
- Log at end: summary counts (updated / skipped / errors).
- Use a consistent prefix: `step-name: 150/1025 processed (42 updated)`.

## Example

```typescript
const PROGRESS_EVERY = 50
for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i += 1) {
  // ... work ...
  const n = i + 1
  if (n % PROGRESS_EVERY === 0 || n === items.length) {
    console.log(`publish-images: ${n}/${items.length} (${uploaded} uploaded, ${skipped} skipped)`)
  }
}
```

Do not rely on per-file `console.log` for every item — that floods the terminal on ~10k files.
